    <string name="basic_guide_title">Basic section introduction</string>
    <string name="basic_guide_message">In the basic section, you need to enter a task name and
        can add a description if needed.\n\nThe task name is the name of the task you want to create.
        This field is required.\n\nThe description is used to add notes about the task you want to complete.
        This field is optional.
    </string>
    <string name="config_guide_title">Configuration  section introduction</string>
    <string name="config_guide_message">The configuration section allows you to configure the difficulty
        level, task type, and completion method.\n\nThe difficulty level represents how hard the
        task is and the rewards that may be received after completion. The available levels are:
        Mortal, Yao, Gui, Mara, Sage, Xian, Deity, and Creation. This feature is still under
        development and is not fully complete yet.\n\nThe task type is used to classify the task.
        Currently, only the default type is supported.\n\nThere are two completion methods: tap and
        timer.\n\nTap: you only need to press the button to complete the task.\n\nTimer: you need to
        wait for a certain amount of time before the task can be completed.\n\nNote: while a timer
        task is running, you cannot complete any other task.
    </string>
    <string name="reward_guide_title">Reward section introduction</string>
    <string name="reward_guide_message">
        Rewards are what you receive after completing a task.\n\nCoin reward is the number of coins
        you receive after completing a task.\n\nExperience reward is the amount of experience you
        receive after completing a task.\n\nItem rewards are items created by you, or keys that are
        automatically created when you create an app block.\n\nKeys are items used to temporarily
        unlock blocked apps. There are currently 8 types of keys, each with a different color and
        unlock duration:\n\nWhite: 10 minutes\nGray: 30 minutes\nGreen: 60 minutes\nBlue:
        120 minutes\nPurple: 240 minutes\nYellow: 480 minutes\nRed: 1440 minutes\nBlack: 10080
        minutes
    </string>
    <string name="block_basic_guide_title">Basic section introduction</string>
    <string name="block_basic_guide_message">
        In the basic section, you can choose the app you want to block.\n\nTap App name or Package
        name to open the app selection dialog.\n\nAfter selecting an app, press the confirm button
        to save your choice.
    </string>
    <string name="block_type_guide_title">Type section introduction</string>
    <string name="block_type_guide_message">
        The block type determines how the system blocks the app.
        \n\nCurrently, only the permanent type is supported.\n\nPermanent means the app will remain
        blocked while the block is active. You can only unlock it temporarily with a key. After the
        unlock time ends, the app will be blocked again automatically.
    </string>
